<!-- KEEP THE audio_service NOTIFICATION ICONS. THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING.

     I deleted this once, reasoning that resource shrinking is not enabled in this
     project so it could not be doing anything. That was wrong, and the evidence
     says so directly:

       WITH this file      notification posted, id=1124, isPlaying=true,
                           artwork 600x600, verified from SystemUI's media panel
       WITHOUT this file   java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: You must specify an
                           icon resource id to build a CustomAction

     So the icons ARE being stripped without it, whatever the gradle config
     suggests — AAPT2 rewrites and prunes resources on its own. The failure is
     silent: audio_service catches the throw, so the notification simply never
     appears and nothing in the app's log says why.

     Measured beats reasoned. Do not delete this file because the build config
     looks like it makes it unnecessary. -->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
  tools:keep="@drawable/audio_service_*" />
